/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 266 0 R
/T (We chose to identify outliers only after performing the dimensionality reduction because the factor scores provide a more meaningful and consolidated view of player performance than any single raw variable. Individual metrics, such as shots, expected goals, passes, or pressures capture only one aspect of behaviour, and a player might appear extreme in one variable but perfectly normal when considering the full multivariate structure. By reducing the data to a small number of principal components, each summarising a broader performance dimension, we were able to evaluate players based on their overall profiles rather than isolated statistics.)
/E (We chose to identify outliers only after performing the dimensionality reduction because the factor scores provide a more meaningful and consolidated view of player performance than any single raw variable. Individual metrics, such as shots, expected goals, passes, or pressures capture only one aspect of behaviour, and a player might appear extreme in one variable but perfectly normal when considering the full multivariate structure. By reducing the data to a small number of principal components, each summarising a broader performance dimension, we were able to evaluate players based on their overall profiles rather than isolated statistics.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
