972 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 305 0 R
/E (While the proposed framework offers a robust quantitative method for identifying market inefficiencies, it is essential to acknowledge the limitations inherent to a purely statistical approach:)
/Pg 60 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
973 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 305 0 R
/E (Tactical Blindness \(Output vs. Role\): The model evaluates players based on output metrics \(what they did\) without context for tactical instructions \(what they were asked to do\). For instance, a striker with low "Playmaking" scores may possess the technical ability to link play but be tactically instructed to remain central and pin opposition defenders. The algorithm interprets this as low involvement or limited skill, whereas a scout would correctly identify it as tactical discipline.)
/Pg 60 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
974 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 305 0 R
/E (The "Intangibles" Gap: Our Factor Analysis captures measurable on-ball actions and defensive work rate but remains blind to critical intangible qualities. Attributes such as off-ball movement, leadership, decision-making under pressure, and adaptability to new environments are vital determinants of transfer success but cannot be fully quantified by event data alone.)
/Pg 60 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
