/Title (Dendrogram Inspection: By analyzing the vertical distances in the dendrogram \(Fig. 17\), we looked for the largest "jump" or gap between merges. A cut-off threshold at a distance of approximately 6.5 naturally segments the data into five distinct groups. Merging beyond this point \(e.g., to 4 clusters\) would force disparate groups together, drastically increasing internal heterogeneity and loss of information.)
/Dest [37 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3026 0 R
>>
endobj
