3060 0 obj
<<
/Title (The model achieved a Root Mean Square Residual \(RMSR\) of 0.087, falling within the acceptable threshold \(< 0.10\) and indicating a good fit. Following this validation, factor scores were computed for each player, quantifying their performance in each of the three dimensions. These scores serve as the input for the subsequent cluster analysis. The histograms below illustrate the distribution of these scores:)
/Dest [32 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3056 0 R
/Next 3061 0 R
>>
endobj
3061 0 obj
<<
/Title (All three histograms show roughly normal distributions, meaning the factor scores are well-balanced across players. The only small observation is that Pure Finishing Threat is slightly more concentrated around the mean, suggesting fewer extreme finishers in the dataset. Overall, the distributions support the stability and interpretability of the components.)
/Dest [32 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3056 0 R
/Prev 3060 0 R
>>
endobj
3062 0 obj
<<
/Title (This rotated factor structure provided a clear, interpretable foundation for constructing player performance scores and subsequently clustering players according to their underlying performance profiles.)
/Dest [31 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3059 0 R
>>
endobj
